From: Ankit Pipalia <ankit@example.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] arm64: dts: qcom: phoenix: enable PS_HOLD restart

Phoenix completes an orderly Linux shutdown for reboot, but the firmware PSCI
reset path does not restart the device.  It remains unavailable until a hard
power cycle and Type-C reattach.

Qualcomm's downstream SM6150 device tree describes PS_HOLD at 0x0c264000.
Expose that register on Phoenix so the in-tree msm-restart driver can provide a
hardware restart path.  Run an explicitly described PS_HOLD handler before the
generic PSCI restart notifier; if PS_HOLD is ineffective, its existing delay
and NOTIFY_DONE return still allow the PSCI fallback to run.

Signed-off-by: Ankit Pipalia <ankit@example.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-phoenix.dts | 7 +++++++
 drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c                  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-phoenix.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-phoenix.dts
index 1..2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-phoenix.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-phoenix.dts
@@ -324,6 +324,13 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&soc {
+	restart@c264000 {
+		compatible = "qcom,pshold";
+		reg = <0x0 0x0c264000 0x0 0x4>;
+	};
+};
+
 &gpu {
 	zap-shader {
 		firmware-name = "qcom/sm7150/phoenix/a615_zap.mbn";
diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c b/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
index 4fa4d74d9b85..a098d1ee1472 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ static int msm_restart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return PTR_ERR(msm_ps_hold);
 
 	devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART,
-				      128, do_msm_poweroff, NULL);
+				      130, do_msm_poweroff, NULL);
 
 	devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_POWER_OFF,
 				      SYS_OFF_PRIO_DEFAULT, do_msm_poweroff,
